1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,944
Monday, seven in the morning.

2
00:00:01,994 --> 00:00:08,136
Aziz logged out of the mobile bank last night, on purpose, because his little nephew plays games on his phone.

3
00:00:08,186 --> 00:00:10,272
Now he needs to pay for his bus pass.

4
00:00:10,322 --> 00:00:13,344
Same phone, same app, but no session.

5
00:00:13,394 --> 00:00:16,200
What must he show to get back in, and in which order?

6
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:21,528
In Lesson 22, Aziz reached level two, and his phone became Trusted.

7
00:00:21,578 --> 00:00:28,656
This lesson starts a new session on that same phone: the password first, then the one-time code, then the verdict.

8
00:00:28,706 --> 00:00:31,056
First, when is a login needed at all?

9
00:00:31,106 --> 00:00:34,152
Only after a logout, or when a renewal fails.

10
00:00:34,202 --> 00:00:40,248
While a session is valid, the app simply renews it, with no password, as Lesson 21 showed.

11
00:00:40,298 --> 00:00:43,920
Aziz logged out, so this morning he needs a real login.

12
00:00:43,970 --> 00:00:46,368
He types his phone number and his password.

13
00:00:46,418 --> 00:00:48,936
The app sends them with his device identifier.

14
00:00:48,986 --> 00:00:53,520
The gateway does one thing before anything else: it checks the password.

15
00:00:53,570 --> 00:00:58,536
It compares the password with the kept digest from Lesson 13, in constant time.

16
00:00:58,586 --> 00:01:04,680
If the number has no customer at all, the gateway still runs a check, against a dummy digest.

17
00:01:04,730 --> 00:01:09,120
The answer is the same as for a wrong password, and it takes the same time.

18
00:01:09,170 --> 00:01:13,032
So nobody can use the login page to learn who is a customer of the bank.

19
00:01:13,082 --> 00:01:14,928
Suppose Aziz types it wrong.

20
00:01:14,978 --> 00:01:21,216
The count of wrong entries goes up, and the platform writes an audit event and an antifraud event.

21
00:01:21,266 --> 00:01:28,968
At the configured limit, the platform locks password login for the configured time, and sends the notice: password login locked.

22
00:01:29,018 --> 00:01:30,504
But a lock is not a block.

23
00:01:30,554 --> 00:01:34,440
No session ends, and the lock ends by itself after that time.

24
00:01:34,490 --> 00:01:36,336
Aziz types it right this time.

25
00:01:36,386 --> 00:01:39,072
Now, why does the password come first, before any code?

26
00:01:39,122 --> 00:01:40,944
Here is my view.

27
00:01:40,994 --> 00:01:43,872
A code costs money, and it lands on a real phone.

28
00:01:43,922 --> 00:01:50,328
If the gateway sent a code to any number that someone typed, a stranger could fill Aziz's phone with codes all night.

29
00:01:50,378 --> 00:01:54,048
So the gateway sends a code only after a correct password.

30
00:01:54,098 --> 00:01:56,640
A person who knows only the number gets nothing.

31
00:01:56,690 --> 00:01:58,512
Now the code.

32
00:01:58,562 --> 00:02:04,368
It comes through TAF, the antifraud service of the mobile operators, from Lesson 12.

33
00:02:04,418 --> 00:02:08,688
TAF sends it by SMS to Aziz's verified number.

34
00:02:08,738 --> 00:02:12,672
The message says it is for a login, and it names the device model.

35
00:02:12,722 --> 00:02:18,216
If TAF is down, the bank's own SMS service sends the code instead.

36
00:02:18,266 --> 00:02:20,424
That login is then marked not scored.

37
00:02:20,474 --> 00:02:25,056
Aziz types the code, and the platform asks TAF for its verdict.

38
00:02:25,106 --> 00:02:27,432
Green: the login continues.

39
00:02:27,482 --> 00:02:29,664
Red: the login is refused.

40
00:02:29,714 --> 00:02:36,744
Yellow, for a customer who was ever at level two: the login waits for consent and a MyID re-check on this phone.

41
00:02:36,794 --> 00:02:41,352
Sometimes TAF says that the device and the SIM card do not match.

42
00:02:41,402 --> 00:02:47,208
Then the app gives Aziz simple advice: use the mobile network, not the café Wi-Fi.

43
00:02:47,258 --> 00:02:49,320
Today the verdict is green.

44
00:02:49,370 --> 00:02:52,248
One more step, because Aziz is at level two.

45
00:02:52,298 --> 00:02:56,808
The app asks for the face check of the phone itself, the one that unlocks his screen.

46
00:02:56,858 --> 00:02:59,736
This is not MyID, and it gives no level.

47
00:02:59,786 --> 00:03:05,064
If it fails, the login stops, and Aziz can try again as the phone allows.

48
00:03:05,114 --> 00:03:11,616
If it passes, the platform sends a face confirmation to TAF, with his personal identification number.

49
00:03:11,666 --> 00:03:13,488
The phone never sees that number.

50
00:03:13,538 --> 00:03:21,432
If TAF does not answer, the login still continues, and the platform sends the confirmation again at the next login.

51
00:03:21,482 --> 00:03:23,688
Now the gateway is satisfied.

52
00:03:23,738 --> 00:03:26,424
It asks Keycloak for a new access grant.

53
00:03:26,474 --> 00:03:31,488
The session gets level two, because Aziz is at level two and this phone is Trusted.

54
00:03:31,538 --> 00:03:33,360
There is no MyID check.

55
00:03:33,410 --> 00:03:35,784
A trusted phone is exactly why.

56
00:03:35,834 --> 00:03:38,160
The only exception is a yellow verdict.

57
00:03:38,210 --> 00:03:44,832
Last, the platform writes an audit event, and sends the event login to the antifraud system of the bank.

58
00:03:44,882 --> 00:03:46,968
Aziz pays for the bus pass.

59
00:03:47,018 --> 00:03:50,136
The whole login took less time than the bus takes to arrive.

60
00:03:50,186 --> 00:03:52,008
To recap.

61
00:03:52,058 --> 00:03:55,632
The password opens the door, and it always comes first.

62
00:03:55,682 --> 00:03:58,824
The code through TAF proves the SIM card.

63
00:03:58,874 --> 00:04:00,864
The verdict scores the attempt.

64
00:04:00,914 --> 00:04:03,744
The phone's own face check confirms the holder.

65
00:04:03,794 --> 00:04:05,616
And then, a new grant.

66
00:04:05,666 --> 00:04:10,176
But all of this leaned on one fact: the platform already knew this phone.

67
00:04:10,226 --> 00:04:14,424
What if the phone is brand new, with Aziz's number and Aziz's password?

68
00:04:14,474 --> 00:04:16,776
Next: login from a new device.
